Database migrations for wellbeing-app, managed by Flask-Migrate (Alembic).

Run from the `backend/` directory with the venv active:

    flask db upgrade           # apply all pending migrations
    flask db downgrade -1      # roll back one migration
    flask db migrate -m "msg"  # auto-generate a new migration from model changes
    flask db current           # show the current applied revision
    flask db history           # show the migration history

The initial schema migration is `versions/0001_initial_schema.py`. Apply it
on a fresh database with `flask db upgrade`.

NOTES
-----
* Migrations are auto-generated from SQLAlchemy models. Always review the
  generated file before committing — autogenerate misses some things
  (CHECK constraints, certain index types, server defaults).
* The CHECK constraint enforcing the anonymity invariant on `checkins`
  is critical to the architectural anonymity guarantee. Do NOT remove it.
* For production deployments, add `flask db upgrade` as a deploy step
  *before* the new app code starts serving traffic.
